## How to flash

Use the MeshCore web flasher, https://flasher.meshcore.io (Chrome or Edge) → **Custom Firmware** → pick the file → **Flash!**

- **ESP32 boards (Heltec V3 and others):** `-upgrade.bin` updates and keeps the node's identity and settings. `-freshInstall-merged.bin` is a fresh install that erases them.
- **nRF52 boards (RAK4631, T114, ...):** the `.zip` is a DFU package (Custom Firmware, use **Enter DFU mode** first if needed, or press the board's DFU/reset button twice). Or put the board in its bootloader and drag the `.uf2` onto the USB drive.
- **Screenless Heltec V3 builds:** `Heltec_v3_repeater_headless`, `Heltec_v3_room_server_headless`, `Heltec_v3_companion_radio_usb_headless`, `Heltec_v3_companion_radio_ble_headless`. Flash them like the normal Heltec V3 files. No display; the OLED is held off from boot to save power.

**After flashing** (serial console at 115200 baud, or remote admin):
- `powersaving on` turns power saving on.
- `get serial.ondemand` should answer `on` (the serial console keeps working while the board sleeps). `set serial.ondemand off` gives EasySkyMesh's stock behaviour.
- `tsim wake [status|modem_reset]` (Heltec V3 / ESP32 with the console on UART0): pulses UART0 TX (GPIO43) low 3 × 20 ms to wake a LilyGO T-SIM wired TX43 → 1N5817 → GPIO6, then sends `@TSIM <CMD> <seq>` over serial until the T-SIM answers `@TSIM ACK <seq>` (5 tries); `tsim last` shows the result. Needs [T-SIM v1.7.7](https://github.com/just-stuff-tm/tsim-remote-updater/releases/tag/v1.7.7) or newer. That firmware ACKs the frames: `WAKE` leaves the modem asleep, `STATUS` sends a status report, `MODEM_RESET` runs modem recovery, and a pulse with no frame is ignored. T-SIM firmware through v1.7.6 treats the wake as a Heltec reboot.

## Remote updates and dashboard (T-SIM)

[tsim-remote-updater](https://github.com/just-stuff-tm/tsim-remote-updater) manages a solar repeater over LTE through a LilyGO T-SIM wired to the Heltec's serial port (telemetry, settings, CLI) and installs these releases over the air. It always uses `Heltec_v3_repeater...-upgrade.bin` (never `-freshInstall-merged`), so identity and settings are kept. Install [T-SIM v1.7.7](https://github.com/just-stuff-tm/tsim-remote-updater/releases/tag/v1.7.7) from the dashboard with **Update T-SIM firmware** before using `tsim wake`.
